course: dictionary
lesson: 11899
title: Accents and place words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you where a person comes from. Brummie is one of these. It is an informal word, so you would use it when talking with friends, not in a formal letter. «Our new teacher is a Brummie from Birmingham.» Here Brummie is a noun, a person from Birmingham.
explain: The word can also describe things. «Sam loves the Brummie way of speaking.» Here Brummie is an adjective, and it means the accent or way of talking of people from Birmingham. You can tell the job of a word by the words around it.
explain: Context clues help here too. «My nan is a Brummie, so she calls me bab.» Bab is a Brummie word, and the sentence shows it is a friendly word for someone you care about. A dictionary explains that it means dear.
fact: Brummie is an informal word, used in the UK.
fact: A Brummie is a person from Birmingham, the big city in the middle of England.
fact: Brummie can also mean the accent and way of speaking of people from Birmingham.
fact: «Bab» is a Brummie word for a friendly «dear».
fact: The name Brummie comes from «Brummagem», an old local name for Birmingham.
exercise: «Our new neighbour is a Brummie, so she was born in Birmingham.» What is a Brummie? | A loud sound in a park | A type of bird from the countryside | *A person from Birmingham | A cake from London
exercise: Mum says «bab» to me with a big smile. What does bab mean here? | A name for a dog | A big, loud shout | *A friendly word like dear | A cross word for a naughty child
exercise: «Lena wore her Brummie football scarf to the match.» What does Brummie describe here? | A large bus | *Something from Birmingham | A teacher | A type of bread
test: Brummagem is an old local name for which city? | Manchester | *Birmingham | London | Bristol
test: Which is true about the word Brummie? | It only means a type of food | It means a friendly dog | *It is informal, and it can mean a person, an accent, or something from Birmingham | It is a formal word used in official letters
exam: Which sentence uses Brummie as an adjective? | «My cousin is a Brummie.» | «Dad is a Brummie from Birmingham.» | *«The Brummie café serves the best cakes.» | «The Brummie accent sounds warm and friendly.»
